    "direct": "The external path helper converts UTF-16 to UTF-8, folds only ASCII capitals and applies 64-bit multiply-before-xor FNV-1 to the complete path. The external lookup compares a 64-bit key in 24-byte rows, with a separate language comparison. The numeric family retains the DWORD descriptor ID and searches ordered twenty-byte key/language rows. Bank codec classes select a populated bank table, otherwise the sound table. The package loop returns its first successful row and writes the row geometry plus retained package pointer; allocation failure terminates the loop. Successful native package load prepends the package; a separate exact package-ID routine moves a matching entry to the head. Removal unlinks and releases one reference, while selected descriptors separately retain the package. Native encrypted-header load and table pointers agree with the offline header reader on the admitted physical cohort.",
